{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1374296-rifts-trinity-continuum","id":1374296,"title":"RIFTS: Trinity Continuum","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-11T21:50:42-07:00","id":1374296,"title":"RIFTS: Trinity Continuum","content":"I have always been a fan of the Rifts by Kevin Siembieda. Could not stand the system but loved the setting. Would make a great Trinity What If?<br /> <br /> <b><i><br /> Nuclear holocaust ignited the destruction of the world as we know it, but it was not the primary instrument of destruction. The sudden destruction of a billion people triggered a surge in the ley lines. All that psychic energy released at once. The sudden influx of psychic energy sent the energy rippling through the mystical crossroads of earth like an earthquake. Ley lines flowed with energy that had not been felt for a million years. The energy surged and pulsed and crisscrossed across the planet at the speed of light. At ley line intersections (nexus points), rifts in space and time tore open, releasing even more energy. The earth shuddered and heaved. Millions more died, increasing the energy level of the rifts. The oceans leapt from their basin and washed over the land. Hundred of millions more died, their psychic energy drawn into the ley lines, and the natural energies doubled again. A chain reaction was unleashed that could not be halted. The continent men called Atlantis leapt from its watery grave and rose to the light of day for the first time in millennia. Its rebirth changing the very face of the planet. In its wake, the eastern coast of the United States was engulfed by the ocean, sending the energy of millions more into the relentless rifts.<br /> <br /> <br /> From the rifts spewed forth energy that tore through man's citadels of steel and concrete like a tornado through a city built out of match sticks. For every million or billion of lives lost, the ley lines surged and destroyed billions more; a nightmare in geometric principles.<br /> <br /> <br /> The ley lines and the rifts that they opened were not some insidious evil, nor a plot of some malignant intelligence from another world. It was an aspect of nature that science did not even know, let alone understand. Like a child playing with matches in a pool of gasoline, humankind dropped a match into the pool and was instantly engulfed. Once the match was lit and dropped, there was nothing that could be done to undo what had been done. Yet in a strange way, all this death was part of the birth of a new age. And through it all, humankind would persevere. Even the cosmic fury of a world gone mad could not completely eradicate all human life. However, it would take mankind hundreds of years to crawl out of the abyss that swallowed him. It is at this moment, as humankind finally crawls back into the light of a new dawn that our story unfolds.<br /> </i></b><br /> <br /> -- RIFTS RPG Core Rulebook","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T03:07:08-07:00","id":1374314,"title":"","content":"I like the artwork in Rifts, but I\u2019ve never played it. Also, my friend just started playing Rifts cause her girlfriend (romantic girlfriend, not friend friend) got her into it. She asked me if I knew of any armor that was functional but still sexy that her character could wear, but I didn\u2019t really know the setting that well. Could you recommend anything?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T03:49:38-07:00","id":1374317,"title":"","content":"I told her about the Glitter Boy armor from the Coalition States, but she thought it looked ridiculously clunky, and I couldn\u2019t think of anything else off the top of my head. She\u2019s played a lot of video games, but this is her first tabletop RPGs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T04:56:57-07:00","id":1374325,"title":"","content":"I have the image of Rifts as Post-Apocalypse Shadowrun. And that is good. Never played Rifts, but played some Shadowrun, enough to say that Rifts sounds fun...<br /> <br /> Question: would you put magic as magic or a variation of Psionic/Quantum/Flux powers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 03-12-2020, 08:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T05:19:36-07:00","id":1374331,"title":"","content":"Rifts has the most broken system I've personally seen in TRPG - it's hell to read. The world itself is fairly interesting, but also kind of a mess. The books are also really shittily formatted. I tried to play it over a decade ago with some friends, but we kinda gave up during the first session. Savage RIFTS looks to be better in every way, but I haven't personally tried it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T05:39:03-07:00","id":1374334,"title":"","content":"As a kid my best friend and I played Rifts for years, but yeah...the system is a total show. I tried to run a new game about a year ago and I could barely finish one session. The kitchen sink setting is fun, but pretty nonsense even by TTRPG standards. That said, I enjoyed the game for years and still have a fondness for it. I've heard good things about the Savage Worlds version and I think I'd try that rather than porting it over to Trinity. That said, I am totally comfortable stealing some of the best bits of the setting for random alternate worlds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T08:24:51-07:00","id":1374352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1374296-rifts-trinity-continuum?p=1374314#post1374314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the artwork in Rifts, but I\u2019ve never played it. Also, my friend just started playing Rifts cause her girlfriend (romantic girlfriend, not friend friend) got her into it. She asked me if I knew of any armor that was functional but still sexy that her character could wear, but I didn\u2019t really know the setting that well. Could you recommend anything?</div> </div> </div> </div>The T-21 Terrain Hopper is a suit of power armor designed primarily for mobility, and is pretty much the opposite of the Glitter Boy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\"