class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1374296-rifts-trinity-continuum?p=1374317#post1374317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I told her about the Glitter Boy armor from the Coalition States, but she thought it looked ridiculously clunky, and I couldn\u2019t think of anything else off the top of my head. She\u2019s played a lot of video games, but this is her first tabletop RPGs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Please keep in mind this is a Trinity Continuum forum: if someone wants to discuss how to adapt RIFTS to the Trinity Continuum rules, cool. If, however, you're looking for recommendations on just playing RIFTS, there are <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?forums/tabletop-roleplaying-open.3/\" target=\"_blank\">better places</a> than this one for that conversation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T10:57:17-07:00","id":1374376,"title":"","content":"As Ian said, what would be your approach of magic?<br /> <br /> my suggestion is kind of: Elemental = Quantum, Rifit/Mystic = Psi and Shifter = Flux","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T12:05:40-07:00","id":1374387,"title":"","content":"I would either go with a psi Which seems to match wrist the closest 2PPE War something new and completely different","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T12:07:22-07:00","id":1374388,"title":"","content":"I also think that the scale mechanic would make the perfect replacement for SDC and MDC Comparrison","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T12:16:06-07:00","id":1374391,"title":"","content":"I'd probably not hew too closely to the TC rules, but you can pull some useful things from them. You can probably slice and dice the Aeon psychic powers into something usable for all of the psionic classes. The VARGS are a big step in the right direction for the power-armor-based classes. The magic-users are probably going to require some new rules, I think. Juicers would get access to scale for speed and strength with a death countdown rule of some kind. Crazies are probably closest to Talents, but that system isn't going to be a perfect fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T12:53:32-07:00","id":1374399,"title":"","content":"Tech is pretty straight forward.<br /> You can create your powered armors / weapons / cybernetics with Aeon rules, maybe add some tags for some weird stuff, I never played, so I never went into details.<br /> <br /> Magic can be as simple as I made in Fists of Flux (spells that are learned and invented one by one), or as complex as reform all the Psionic system to be more flexible (they learn a base effect and use it as required). Aberrant rules are too powerful, unless you limit scale to a limit and focus on power tags. that's a good option for elemental and most other powers indeed, but it would work more like magical power than spells (as D&amp;D and Ars Magica spells).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz